{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read the human's request in /runtime/task/SPEC.md; it may be rough notes rather than a complete draft. Use the spec-template skill to investigate the project and draft or refine /runtime/task/SPEC.md. Preserve existing human intent, constraints, and substantive content; never overwrite it with a blank template. Record unresolved questions rather than inventing requirements. Incorporate previous review feedback. Write the updated SPEC.md to disk. Do not implement code or approve documents. The application workspace is the current working directory supplied by Watts; the package descriptor may live elsewhere. Implement application source, tests, modules, and other project files in the project root and its normal source directories. The task directory holds workflow documents, story logs, review artifacts, and execution evidence only; do not create application code or a separate application module inside it. Quality gates run from the project root, not with a task-directory working directory.\nTask documents are in /runtime/task. Application work belongs in /workspace. Write the requested task outputs to /runtime/task."}],"timestamp":1791815345139}}
